  "question": {
    "text": "If $10 \\sin ^4 \\theta+15 \\cos ^4 \\theta=6$, then the value of $\\frac{27 \\operatorname{cosec}^6 \\theta+8 \\sec ^6 \\theta}{16 \\sec ^8 \\theta}$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ub5km",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UJNDu",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QU0US",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ABC4U",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 10\\left(\\sin ^2 \\theta\\right)^2+15\\left(1-\\sin ^2 \\theta\\right)^2=6 \\\\ & \\text { Let } \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\mathrm{t} \\Rightarrow 10 \\mathrm{t}^2+15(1-\\mathrm{t})^2=16 \\\\ & 10 \\mathrm{t}^2+15-30 \\mathrm{t}+15 \\mathrm{t}^2=6 \\\\ & 25 \\mathrm{t}^2-30 \\mathrm{t}+9=0 \\\\ & (5 \\mathrm{t}-3)^2=0 \\\\ & \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\frac{3}{5} \\text { and } \\cos ^2 \\theta=\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ & \\frac{27 \\times \\frac{125}{27}+8+\\frac{125}{8}}{16\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^4}=\\frac{250}{125 \\times 5}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
